Description: unisoc plugin -- Unisoc SoC modems over SIPC (E5)
 The AT port is the WWAN port of the kernel's sipc_wwan driver, the data path
 the sipa_eth interface.  The generic modem, except:
  - no ATZ and no +CPMS=: either silences the CP's AT server until a reboot.
    The core gains MMBroadbandModemClass.sms_storages_fixed: storage locks
    succeed, without a command, only for the storages +CPMS? reported;
  - capabilities (GSM/UMTS, LTE, 5G NR) and IP families (IPv4, IPv6, IPv4v6)
    stated, not probed: +GCAP says +CGSM and +CGDCONT=? "IP" only;
  - signal from all nine +CESQ fields (NR included), and from the +CESQ the
    modem reports unsolicited; its unsolicited +CSQ is swallowed;
  - the SMS service centre written back once per boot (+CSCA=, the value
    +CSCA? reports): until then every submit fails with +CMS ERROR: 313;
  - the dial's "+CDU:" and the call reports (^DSCI, +CLCCS, ...) swallowed,
    calls followed through +CLCC polling;
  - a bearer that activates the context (+CGACT), routes it to the net port
    (+CGDATA="M-ETHER") and reads its settings from +CGCONTRDP: IPv4 static,
    IPv6 by router advertisement with the DNS servers of the dotted IPv6 line.
Author: e5-linux
Forwarded: not-needed

